* controllers.lib - Generalized Control Modules for SPICE
* This library contains universal parameterized subcircuits for different control architectures.

* -----------------------------------------------------------
* PEAK CURRENT MODE CONTROLLER (PCMC)
* -----------------------------------------------------------
* Inputs: 
*   v_out   : Sensed output voltage
*   v_ref   : Reference voltage
*   i_sense : Voltage signal proportional to inductor current (1V = 1A if RSENSE=1)
* Outputs:
*   pwm_out : Gate drive signal (0V or 1V)
*   ctrl    : Internal PI control voltage (current setpoint)
*   ramp    : Slope compensation ramp voltage
* Parameters:
*   KP      : Proportional gain (outer voltage loop)
*   KI      : Integral gain (outer voltage loop)
*   M_SLOPE : Slope compensation (V/s) to prevent sub-harmonic oscillation
*   RSENSE  : Current sense gain (V/A)
*   F_SW    : Switching frequency (Hz)
* -----------------------------------------------------------
.subckt PCMC_CONTROLLER v_out v_ref i_sense pwm_out ctrl ramp PARAMS: KP=0.01 KI=0.001 M_SLOPE=0 RSENSE=1 F_SW=100k

* 1. Outer Voltage Loop (PI Controller)
Eerr err 0 value = { v(v_ref) - v(v_out) }
Bint 0 int_val I={ v(err) * KI }
Cint int_val 0 100u IC=0.5
Rint int_val 0 10MEG

* Anti-windup for PI
Dclamp1 int_val clamp_high D_ideal
Dclamp2 clamp_low int_val D_ideal
Vclamp_high clamp_high 0 DC 0.9
Vclamp_low clamp_low 0 DC 0.01

* Control Voltage (Current Command)
Ectrl ctrl 0 value = { v(err) * KP + v(int_val) < 0.01 ? 0.01 : (v(err) * KP + v(int_val) > 0.9 ? 0.9 : v(err) * KP + v(int_val)) }

* 2. Slope Compensation
* Ramp from 0 to M_SLOPE/F_SW
Vramp ramp 0 PULSE(0 {M_SLOPE/F_SW} 0 {0.99/F_SW} {0.01/F_SW} 0 {1/F_SW})
E_vc_eff vc_eff 0 value = { v(ctrl) - v(ramp) }

* 3. Inner Current Loop (Comparator)
Ecomp comp 0 value = { v(i_sense) * RSENSE >= v(vc_eff) ? 1 : 0 }

* 4. SR Latch for PWM
* Clock sets the latch (turns switch ON) at the start of every cycle
Vclk clk 0 PULSE(0 1 0 1n 1n {0.05/F_SW} {1/F_SW})

* Analog latch implementation using controlled current sources and a 100pF capacitor
* Reset dominates if comp goes high immediately
B_set 0 state I = { (v(clk) > 0.5) * (v(comp) <= 0.5) }
B_res state 0 I = { (v(comp) > 0.5) }
C_state state 0 100p IC=0
D1 state clamp_h D_ideal
D2 clamp_l state D_ideal
V_h clamp_h 0 DC 1
V_l clamp_l 0 DC 0

* 5. Output Buffer
Epwm pwm_out 0 value = { v(state) > 0.5 ? 1 : 0 }

.model D_ideal D(N=0.001 RS=0.001)
.ends PCMC_CONTROLLER
